      "text": "To find the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we first identify the first term and the common ratio of the series. The first term \\(a\\) is 1, and the common ratio \\(r\\) is 2.\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by the formula:\n\\[\nS_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\n\\]\nHere, the series has 11 terms (since \\(1024 = 2^{10}\\)), so \\(n = 11\\). Substituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[\nS_{11} = 1 \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1\n\\]\nNow, we calculate \\(2^{11}\\):\n\\[\n2^{11} = 2048\n\\]\nTherefore, the sum is:\n\\[\nS_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047\n\\]\nThe sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is \\(\\boxed{2047}\\).",
